+# LumberLands 0.3.1 — LT2 tree parity / collision / jitter hotfix
+
+This pass is a correction to 0.3.0. It keeps the working unified tree entity and Neon renderer, but removes several 0.3.0 approximations that were visibly wrong in game.
+
+## Reference basis
+
+- User-provided `LumberTycoon2.rbxl` and `LT2(2).rbxl`.
+- The supplied LT2 `TreeSubclasses/CaveCrawler` and `TreeSuperClass` source recovered from the place file.
+- User screenshots from the 0.3.0 test showing the global warm/red cast, ground clipping, inaccurate walk collision and loose-piece jitter.
+- Frost post-dates the supplied 2017 place. For Frost only, current LT2 documentation/thumbnail is used: white SmoothPlastic bark, Ice cyan inner wood, Glass cyan leaves, Oak-like but more erratic growth, and Lava/Volcano-like leaves on outer extremities.
+
+## Fixed
+
+### 1. Global red/brown tree tint
+
+0.3.0 multiplied each RGB channel of Roblox's legacy material color map by the requested LT2 BrickColor. That preserves the source material image's own hue and was contaminating the requested color, producing the visible red/brown cast across unrelated tree species.
+
+0.3.1 keeps only the material map's luminance/detail and applies the LT2 BrickColor as the actual hue. Foil's normal-derived detail path and Neon's emissive/fullbright path are preserved.
+
+### 2. Ghost hitbox after a tree is chopped down
+
+Standing-tree geometry/collision is now synchronized immediately when sections are detached instead of waiting until the next tree tick. `Lt2TreeVisualEntity` also removes itself from the active collision index immediately when discarded and clears its cached collision boxes.
+
+### 3. Loose wood ground jitter / repeated floor clipping
+
+The 0.3.0 terrain solver intentionally projected only 82% of a penetration and capped each correction to 0.20 blocks. Gravity then pushed the same body back into the floor on the next substep, creating the reported clip -> push-up -> clip loop.
+
+0.3.1 projects the body fully out to a tiny collision slop, gives small pieces more contact iterations, and allows a much larger one-step correction when necessary. Ordinary loose trees now also use every visible section for terrain contact up to 72 sections; only genuinely giant bodies use a reduced structural contact set.
+
+### 4. Walk collision now follows the actual branch much more closely
+
+0.3.0 approximated a rotated limb with AABB slices as long as 0.82 blocks. On an angled section those boxes contain a large amount of empty space above the rendered cuboid, which is why the player could stand/flo​​at above the tree.
+
+0.3.1 uses 0.10–0.20 block collision slices with no outward inflation. In addition, standing and loose trees run a final server-authoritative OBB penetration/support pass against the same rotated cuboids used by the LT2 tree graph. Moving logs use all sections—not just the mass-dominant terrain subset—for player support.
+
+### 5. Cave Crawler no longer uses the made-up 0.3.0 morphology
+
+The 0.3.0 "modern calibration" is removed. Cave Crawler is restored directly to the values in the supplied LT2 ModuleScript, including:
+
+- GrowInterval: 1–3
+- MaxGrowCalls: 120–200
+- NewBranchCutoff: 10
+- BarkThickness: 1.5
+- SeedThickness: 0.08–0.10
+- ThicknessGrow: 0.08–0.10
+- LengthGrow: 0.04–0.08
+- Trunk split distance: 1–3
+- Later split distance: 30–80
+- Split count: 2–6
+- Split angle: 0–60
+- Bend distance: 8–13
+- Bend angle: 10–30
+- Leaves: 2–5 Mulberry/Foil parts
+- LeafSizeFactor: X 4–6, Y 3–4, Z 4–6
+
+The Cavecrawler/Frost special case that incorrectly treated leaf size factors as absolute studs is removed. LT2's TreeSuperClass behavior—leaf size factors scale with the parent section thickness—is used again.
+
+This also removes the artificial "fixed-looking" Cavecrawler base/fork behavior from 0.3.0. The stump/first fork is procedural from LT2's source ranges rather than being shape-tuned into one silhouette.
+
+### 6. Frost morphology corrected
+
+Frost is not present in the supplied old place because it was added later. 0.3.0 nevertheless invented a sparse angular generator with almost no normal branching and absolute-size leaf slabs. That does not match current LT2 references.
+
+0.3.1 instead follows the documented Frost target: an Oak-like but more erratic structure, white SmoothPlastic bark, Ice cyan interior, and sparse Lava/Volcano-like Glass leaf pads only on surviving outer extremities. Its low-friction loose-wood behavior remains intact.
+
+## Preserved
+
+- Unified `Lt2TreeVisualEntity` architecture.
+- Server-authoritative growth/cutting/rigid-body tree graph.
+- Working Neon fullbright/emissive pass and real Minecraft light proxies.
+- LT2 cut marks and cut faces.
+- Re-chopping loose wood.
+- Tree grab/drag system and mass behavior.
+- Fabric, Forge, NeoForge and universal project targets for Minecraft 1.21.1.
+
+## Validation performed in this workspace
+
+- All JSON resources parse successfully.
+- Modified Java sources were passed through `javac` parsing; no Java parser/syntax diagnostics were produced before dependency-resolution errors.
+- Direct 0.3.0 -> 0.3.1 diffs were reviewed for the tree registry, runtime physics/collision, visual entity collision cache and Roblox material generation task.
+
+## Build limitation
+
+This source archive does not include a Gradle wrapper and this workspace has no Gradle installation/dependency cache, so a real Minecraft loader compile/JAR launch cannot be performed here. Build 0.3.1 on the normal development machine and test the four reported behaviors first: tree color, ghost collision after felling, a single loose log resting on flat ground, and walking along a strongly angled branch.
